# Drift/QA capture output — regenerate with `npx playwright test e2e/driftCapture.spec.mjs`
hostv2/review-shots/drift/

# Ad-hoc QA screenshots dropped at the repo root by a live drive. They are
# throwaway evidence, not artifacts — 11 of them (~4MB) accumulated untracked
# before this rule existed. Durable captures belong in hostv2/review-shots/.
/*.png

# hostv2 DEPLOY ARTIFACT — Model A (2026-08-03). Generated, never committed.
# It was tracked so a laptop-built gh-pages branch would carry it, guarded by a
# byte-exact drift gate. That gate assumed vite output is reproducible; it is,
# on ONE machine — CI building the same source produced HostShellV2-4c0ca35e.js
# against a committed d448e983, so the gate could never go green on a PR. Both
# release paths now BUILD it: `npm run release` (which predeploy runs) and the
# from-source Pages workflow. Regenerate locally with `npm run sync:hostv2`.
/public/hostv2/

# Throwaway self-signed certs for LAN phone testing (HTTPS=1 npx vite --host).
# A private key is never committed, even a disposable one.
hostv2/.certs/
